506
00:31:11,260 --> 00:31:16,025
and he said he was sorry, what's done is
done, no point in going on about it now.

507
00:31:18,260 --> 00:31:20,720
That hurt, good, it proves you're alive.

508
00:31:21,580 --> 00:31:22,815
Alright, fair enough.

509
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:31,577
Look at the stars, a sea of
lights spreading out forever,

510
00:31:31,660 --> 00:31:34,417
I wonder if Laboon is
looking up at the same stars.

511
00:31:34,500 --> 00:31:36,277
What do you think, Captain?

512
00:31:36,360 --> 00:31:41,257
Hey guys, come look, Brooke's
getting emotional out here.

513
00:31:41,340 --> 00:31:44,980
I was being sincere, don't make fun of me.

514
00:31:48,180 --> 00:31:50,157
It's the marines, what do we do?

515
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:53,020
Same thing we always do, give them hell.

516
00:31:54,700 --> 00:31:59,420
Damn, look at that, Captain, Yorkie's
bounty went up again, he's on a roll.

517
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:07,737
Eat that, let's celebrate with a song,
Yorkie, Yorkie, a bounty on his head.

518
00:32:07,820 --> 00:32:11,232
Out the twin cape flies the
news, the navy wants his head.

519
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:33,420
Bad news, men!

520
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:35,377
There's something wrong with the captain.

521
00:32:35,460 --> 00:32:36,757
He ain't looking so good.

522
00:32:36,840 --> 00:32:38,400
I'm serious! Huh?

523
00:32:42,080 --> 00:32:43,100
A virus?

524
00:32:45,500 --> 00:32:46,330
I'm afraid so.

525
00:32:46,413 --> 00:32:47,497
Everyone stay out.

526
00:32:47,580 --> 00:32:49,874
We've got a dozen men infected already.

527
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:55,697
I figure they must have contracted it
when we passed through that jungle.

528
00:32:55,780 --> 00:32:57,721
I've never seen anything like it.

529
00:32:57,820 --> 00:32:59,397
None of my treatments work.

530
00:32:59,480 --> 00:33:01,362
We've all got to be careful now.

531
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:06,280
If this plague keeps spreading, we
won't have enough men to sail this ship.

532
00:33:10,520 --> 00:33:12,285
Please hang in there, Captain.

533
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:15,240
Come on, don't sound so depressed.

534
00:33:18,520 --> 00:33:20,457
We're the Rumbar Pirates, remember?

535
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:22,680
We bring smiles to children's faces.

536
00:33:23,280 --> 00:33:28,104
Though I admit I've seen better days, and
that goes for the rest of the ship, too.

537
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:31,657
I'm sorry I won't be able to
travel the Grand Line with you.

538
00:33:31,740 --> 00:33:33,446
We'll have to part ways here.

539
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:38,057
I'll take this ship, but I want all
of you to move forward with a new one.

540
00:33:38,140 --> 00:33:38,970
Captain, no.

541
00:33:39,540 --> 00:33:43,481
We can't risk the infection spreading
any more than it already has.

542
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:44,737
We'll drop you off.

543
00:33:44,820 --> 00:33:49,408
Try passing through the Calm Belt and
look for help for the sick crew members.

544
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:52,060
It'll all work out somehow, I hope.

545
00:33:53,100 --> 00:33:54,480
I'm sorry, guys.

546
00:33:54,900 --> 00:33:56,440
Give Laboon my regards.

547
00:33:58,080 --> 00:33:59,380
Wipe those tears away.

548
00:33:59,640 --> 00:34:01,240
Stand up straight. Yes.

549
00:34:05,120 --> 00:34:05,950
Brooke?

550
00:34:06,400 --> 00:34:07,230
Yes.

551
00:34:18,960 --> 00:34:20,200
Give them hope.

552
00:34:22,020 --> 00:34:23,997
I will, my captain!

553
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:26,437
I swear, as long as I live!

554
00:34:26,520 --> 00:34:28,337
I will never forget those words.

555
00:34:28,420 --> 00:34:30,140
Hey, hear that?

556
00:34:30,380 --> 00:34:32,204
I've engraved them in my heart.

557
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:34,917
Captain, we'll meet again!

558
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,080
So take care.

559
00:34:36,780 --> 00:34:38,977
We may be parting ways now?

560
00:34:39,060 --> 00:34:40,357
But this isn't the end!

561
00:34:40,440 --> 00:34:42,257
So please don't die.

562
00:34:42,340 --> 00:34:44,217
Take off that mask.

563
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:45,737
Let me see your face.

564
00:34:45,820 --> 00:34:49,000
We'll all sing together again someday.

565
00:34:58,540 --> 00:34:59,540
Hey Brooke.

566
00:35:00,660 --> 00:35:01,717
While you're here.

567
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:04,180
Why don't you send me off

568
00:35:05,040 --> 00:35:06,640
With my favorite song?

569
00:35:20,220 --> 00:35:22,677
Gather up all of the crew.

570
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:25,437
It's time to ship out Binx's brew.

571
00:35:25,520 --> 00:35:28,077
Sea wind blows to where?

572
00:35:28,160 --> 00:35:30,857
Who knows the waves will be our guide?

573
00:35:30,940 --> 00:35:34,360
Or across the ocean's tide?
